# SdfFileFormat Json plugin (C++)

This package is an example of how to write an SdfFileFormat plugin in C++.

## Key details

- In `plugInfo.json`, we use `@PLUG_INFO_LIBRARY_PATH@`, `@PLUG_INFO_RESOURCE_PATH@`, and `@PLUG_INFO_ROOT@` to allow our plugin to be used in both SwiftUsd-based apps and vanilla OpenUSD-based runtimes.
- In `Package.swift`, we use `.copy("plugInfo.json")` and `.plugin(name: "generate-plug-info-json", package: "SwiftUsd")` to have the build system fill in the `@PLUG_INFO_*@` values based on the target architecture
- In `fileFormat.hpp`, we subclass from `pxr::SdfFileFormat` and override/implement some of its virtual methods.
- In `fileFormat.cpp`, we use the `TF_REGISTRY_FUNCTION` macro along with `SDF_DEFINE_FILE_FORMAT` to tell the OpenUSD runtime how to use our custom plugin.

## Usage
To use this plugin in a SwiftUsd-based app:
1. Add it as a package dependency to your Swift Package/Xcode project.

To use this plugin in a vanilla OpenUSD-based app:
1. `cd` into the package directory
2. Run `swift build`
3. Run `swift package build-vanilla-openusd-plugin` and note the outputed plugin path
4. Set the `PXR_PLUGINPATH_NAME` environment variable to point to your plugin. For example:
```
export PXR_PLUGINPATH_NAME="/Users/maddyadams/SwiftUsd/Examples/SdfFileFormat/hioJson_Cxx/.build/plugins/build-vanilla-openusd-plugin/outputs/sdfJson.usdplugin/:$PXR_PLUGINPATH_NAME"
usdcat example.usda -o example.json
usdcat example.json -o example2.usda
```

## Code structure
- `fileFormat.hpp`/`fileFormat.cpp` contains `class SdfJsonFileFormat: public pxr::SdfFileFormat`. It uses `pxr::JsValue` to handle Json parsing/printing, and calls into `readLayer` and `writeLayer` in `CoreSpecSerialization.hpp`. 
- `CoreSpecSerialization.hpp`/`CoreSpecSerialization.cpp` handles the reading and writing of layers, prims, attributes, and relationships. 
- `LIVERPSSerialization.hpp`/`LIVERPSSerialization.cpp` handles the reading and writing of composition arcs. 
- `SdfSerialization.hpp`/`SdfSerialization.cpp` handles the reading and writing of other `Sdf` types. 
- `TfSerialization.hpp`/`TfSerialization.cpp` handles the reading and writing of `Tf` types. 
- `TsSerialization.hpp`/`TsSerialization.cpp` handles the reading and writing of `Ts` (spline) types. 
- `VtSerialization.hpp`/`VtSerialization.cpp` handles the reading and writing of `Vt` types. Particular care is taken with `VtValue` to ensure that USD files can be losslessly converted into Json and back to USD. 